{"id": 25, "ts": 1780643776.2151048, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s clarification that Candidate\u202fB has a relatively weak memory for numbers. That does raise a legitimate concern for the attention\u2011and\u2011information\u2011accuracy criterion, especially on long\u2011haul routes where precise fuel, altitude, and timing calculations are critical. However, when we weigh this against the other candidates, the trade\u2011off remains in B\u2019s favor. Candidate\u202fA still lacks crew\u2011cooperation and openness to feedback; Candidate\u202fC\u2019s communication deficits and egocentric style could jeopardize cockpit coordination; Candidate\u202fD\u2019s moody, loner temperament similarly threatens crew cohesion. B\u2019s core strengths\u2014high operational reliability, strong stress resilience, solid technical judgment (weather assessment, computer proficiency)\u2014are essential for safety, and his memory weakness can be mitigated through procedural cross\u2011checks and cockpit resource management training. Therefore, I maintain my provisional recommendation for Candidate\u202fB, while flagging the need for targeted support on numerical accuracy."}
